app.degraded	app entered degraded (observe window failure / post-window instability / W_DEPLOY_INSTABILITY)	release-semantics §2.7
app.deleted	app deletion completed (tombstone second beat: managed services removed, name enters retention hold)	B6/H10 added during implementation (MG-3; app deletion second-beat terminal event)
app.instability_detected	instability detected at runtime	release-semantics §2.7
app.recovered	app left degraded, back to running	release-semantics §2.7
app.substrate_missing	app claimed running but its managed service(s) are absent from the substrate (external removal); view corrected to down	T0-V2.2 added during implementation (R2; runtime existence reconciliation: running app whose substrate service vanished — disclosed and the derived view corrected)
app.webhook_fetch_failed	async source fetch failed after webhook acceptance (retry manually via redeliver on the same delivery)	S17-D1 added during implementation (review class D; disclosure of webhook async source-fetch failure)
backup.upload_failed	remote state backup upload failed (local snapshot unaffected; payload carries the backup id and a redacted error summary, never credentials)	E3 object-storage §2.3/D-S3-4 added during implementation (W3-S2 upload track; local snapshot unaffected, payload carries backup id + redacted error summary)
backup.upload_recovered	remote state backup upload recovered (previous upload had failed; payload carries the backup id)	E3 object-storage §2.3/D-S3-4 added during implementation (W3-S2 upload track; red-to-green closure after a failed upload)
build.stale_nonterminal	build stayed queued/building past 2x the build timeout budget (surfaces state-machine bugs; no self-healing)	S18-A10 added during implementation (review class A; over-age alert for non-terminal builds)
cron.failed	cron run failed (task failed/rejected; no retry — restart-condition=none; job service removed)	E5 Cron added during implementation (object-storage §8; W3-S5; run failed, no retry)
cron.skipped	cron trigger skipped (overlap / node unavailable / missed during downtime / interrupted by restart); no catch-up run	architecture §4.3
cron.succeeded	cron run completed (task complete; job service removed)	E5 Cron added during implementation (object-storage §8; W3-S5; run completed, job service removed)
cron.timed_out	cron run exceeded its watchdog budget (default 10m, fleetly.cron.timeout label overrides; job service removed)	E5 Cron added during implementation (object-storage §8; FZ-4 pinned name; watchdog budget exceeded, job service removed)
cron.triggered	cron schedule fired: one-shot swarm job created (payload carries app/service/run id/job service; scheduled_at is the hit cron point)	E5 Cron added during implementation (object-storage §8; W3-S5; one-shot job created on schedule or manual trigger)
db.backup_failed	database backup failed (failure summary in payload, never credentials)	E4 managed-databases §5.3 (operation event; never credentials in payload)
db.backup_succeeded	database backup succeeded (ledger row written; verify pending)	E4 managed-databases §5.3 (operation event; ledger row written)
db.credentials_rotated	database credentials rotated (manual two-phase confirm; referencing apps auto-redeploy follows)	E4 managed-databases §5.3 (operation event; referencing apps auto-redeploy follows)
db.degraded	database in service turned unhealthy (health probe failing / task crash loop; swarm self-healing observed)	E4 managed-databases §5.3 (transition event; in-service unhealthy)
db.delete_started	database deletion accepted (reference guard passed; tombstone first beat)	E4 managed-databases §5.3 (transition event; reference guard passed, tombstone first beat)
db.deleted	database deletion completed (managed objects reaped; name enters retention hold; volumes orphaned by default)	E4 managed-databases §5.3 (transition event; reap completed, name enters retention hold)
db.provision_failed	database convergence failed (health gate timeout / image unavailable / engine error; scene preserved, explicit retry required)	E4 managed-databases §5.3 (transition event; convergence failed, scene preserved)
db.provision_started	database provisioning/convergence started (create, resume or retry acceptance; state -> provisioning)	E4 managed-databases §5.3 (transition event; provisioning acceptance for create/resume/retry)
db.ready	database passed the health gate (provisioning -> ready)	E4 managed-databases §5.3 (transition event; health gate passed)
db.recovered	database recovered (health probe passing again; degraded -> ready)	E4 managed-databases §5.3 (transition event; degraded -> ready)
db.restore_completed	database restore completed in place (confirm-gated destructive operation)	E4 managed-databases §5.3 (operation event; in-place restore finished)
db.restore_failed	database restore failed (critical alert; in-place replay interrupted)	E4 managed-databases §5.3 (operation event; interrupted in-place restore alerts critically)
db.resumed	database resume accepted (paused -> provisioning reconvergence)	E4 managed-databases §5.3 (transition event; paused -> provisioning)
db.suspended	database suspended (scale 0, services and volumes retained)	E4 managed-databases §5.3 (transition event; ready/degraded -> paused)
db.upgrade_available	newer template image digest available for the database template (opt-in upgrade advertised)	E4 managed-databases §5.3 (operation event; opt-in upgrade advertised)
db.upgrade_failed	database upgrade failed (digest rolled back to the previous value; state degraded)	E4 managed-databases §5.3 (operation event; digest rolled back, state degraded)
db.upgrade_finished	database upgrade finished (new digest converged and healthy)	E4 managed-databases §5.3 (operation event; upgrade converged and healthy)
db.upgrade_started	database upgrade started (pre_upgrade backup gate begins; controlled rebuild)	E4 managed-databases §5.3 (operation event; controlled rebuild with backup gate)
